WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
why you'd be a good person to hire.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.600
When it comes to resumes, there is no one standard formatter template to use, though there

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.800
are many templates available online if you need help starting out.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.700
Most resumes do, however, contain certain standard sections and information.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.400
It's always good to include a cover letter along with your resume.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.000
If you think of a resume as a summary of information and facts about yourself, a cover letter is

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.100
an opportunity to expand on that information, as well as create a personalized message about

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.300
why you want the job, why you're interested in the company, and most importantly, why you

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.000
would be the best person to hire.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.200
As a rule of thumb, try to keep your resume to two pages or less in your cover letter to

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.000
no longer than one page.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.500
Here are a few general tips for preparing a resume and cover letter.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.100
Think spelling and grammar carefully.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:55.800
With so much competition for jobs, spelling and grammatical errors are an easy way for

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.300
those hiring to eliminate applicants since it shows a lack of attention to detail.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.800
Your objective with your resume should be to sell yourself.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.400
Use it to show your strengths, skills, accomplishments, and abilities.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.000
You want your resume to make you stand out from others.
